  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 74,
  "created_at": "2025-11-19T20:05:54.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 18603,
  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Debugging Challenge: Fix the Glitchy Store\r\nThe Tech Gear store is having a data crisis! The **\"Headphones\"** are showing the wrong picture, and the **\"Camera\"** doesn’t have a price at all.\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n\r\n1. **Investigate:** Run the code and look closely for data mismatches. Which items don’t look right?\r\n\r\n2. **Fix the Data:** Examine the arrays used and look for array length issues, hard-coded indices, or mismatched fields\r\n\r\n:::details [<i class=\"fa fa-clipboard\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Debugging Checklist**]\r\n- Did I run the program first to observe the actual issue?  \r\n- Do all arrays have the same length?  \r\n- Are the indices correctly aligned across arrays (item 0 → image 0 → price 0)?  \r\n- Am I accidentally hard-coding an index somewhere?  \r\n- Did I check for typos in array items or variable names?  \r\n- After making a fix, did I run the code again to see if the issue changed?\r\n:::\r\n\r\n3. **Consult with AI:** Ask targeted debugging questions to help you narrow down what’s going wrong.\r\n\r\n**Verify:**  \r\nRun the code again. Do all three products now show the correct **names**, **pictures**, and **prices**?\r\n",
    "submittable": "false",
    "hide_share_and_remix": "false",
    "widget_view": "false",
    "initial_view_mode": "split",
    "disable_edit_run_for_submission": "false",
    "ai_tutor_mode": "engineer",
    "predict_settings": {
      "isPredictLevel": false,
